  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1217 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nA strong upper level high will spin over the Central Rockies and \nCentral Plains through mid week then shift west late week into this \nweekend. As for the short range forecast, expect mostly clear skies \nwith periods of high clouds. Dry conditions are expected with winds \nfrom a southerly direction. Highs through tomorrow will reach into \nthe low 100s with lows tonight and tomorrow night in the 70s. The \nmain concern will be the heat indices that are expected to reach at \nor above 105 degrees. A few places across central Kansas may exceed \n110 degrees. A heat advisory as been issued to account for this. \n\nMid range models show increasing chances of thunderstorms Monday \nnight through Thursday night as weak disturbances move through the \narea. The best chance of precipitation currently look to be across \nfar western Kansas and northern Kansas. Otherwise expect an increase \nin cloud cover. Highs Tuesday through this weekend look to reach \ninto the 90s to low 100s with lows in the upper 60s to upper\n70s.",
